    "result_text": "The build passes with the sole test class (`AcceptanceTest`) green. The successful compile also confirms `OwnerDto.AgeBandEnum.fromValue(...)` resolves against the OpenAPI-generated DTO.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `birthDate` \u2192 `ageBand` feature on `POST /api/owners`, following the existing derived-field conventions in this Spring PetClinic app.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**\n   - Added optional `birthDate` (ISO `date`) to the `OwnerFields` request schema.\n   - Added read-only `ageBand` enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` response schema.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`**\n   - Added the persistent `birthDate` column with getter/setter.\n   - Added `@Transient getAgeBand()` computing the band from `birthDate` measured against `registrationDate` (falling back to `now()` defensively): `< 18 \u2192 MINOR`, `18\u201364 \u2192 ADULT`, `\u2265 65 \u2192 SENIOR`; returns `null` (field omitted) when no birth date is present.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**\n   - Added an explicit `ageBand` mapping (String \u2192 `OwnerDto.AgeBandEnum`), mirroring the existing `contactPreference` expression pattern. `birthDate` flows in automatically via the existing `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` mapping.\n\n4. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column (hsqldb is what the tests use; others updated for consistency).\n\nThe `coreDerivesAgeBand` acceptance test (birthDate `1990-01-01`, registered today `2026-08-11` \u2192 `ADULT`) passes, and the full suite is green.\n\nNote: since `registrationDate` can be back-dated by the client on create (up to today), the spec's \"computed against registrationDate\" is honored exactly \u2014 the age band reflects age as of the registration date, not the current date.",
